   "source": [
    "- its puproose is to remove overfitting from the data .\n",
    "- L1 and L2 also works as individual models as well.\n",
    "- genralised model - highly desirable.\n",
    "- cost function = error term.\n",
    "- penalising term which is responsible for twiking of the slope.\n",
    "- equation of lr :- cost function\n",
    "    mean square error of 1 = (y_test - y_pred) whole sq. + .......\n",
    "    ->mean square error for many values = summation of (i=1 and n) ((h0 (x)power i - (y)power i ))whole sq. + lamda(slope)whole sq.\n",
    "    Here, lamda(slope)whole sq. is responsible for twiking the  slope & lamda is the penalising term.\n",
    "    we will find the lamda by using hit and tiral method and if we want the optical value of the lamda then we will use hyperparameter tuning.\n",
    "\n",
    "- slope = B0 + B1X1 + B2X2 +...+ BnXn + c.\n",
    "- here we have good degree change of the slope.\n",
    "- L2 = ridge regualrisation.\n",
    "- L1 = Lasso regularisation.\n",
    "- this was for L2 regularisation.\n",
    "- Now for L1 Regualarisation.\n",
    "- cost function = (h0(x)power i - (y)power i)whole sq.\n",
    "    = summmation(n & i=1) , (h0(x)power i-(y)power i)whole sq. + lamda|slope|\n",
    "    here we will multiply the slope.\n",
    "- in L1 regularisation the twiking happens very slowly.\n",
    "- here the slope twiks little bit."
   ]
  },
